[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-93
TITLE: Emission Indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that an accepted direct emission start enables the external indicators only when
the required interlocks are ready, and that an emission stop disables the indicators.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to accept direct emission start and stop directives.
2. The required readiness inputs can be placed in their good and bad conditions.
3. The external indicator output, audible indicator, on-board LED6, and queued HVPS
   commands can be observed.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Confirm the external indicators and LED6 are inactive.
2. Place every required readiness input in its good condition and issue a start directive.
3. Observe the external indicators, LED6, and queued HVPS command.
4. Issue a stop directive and observe the same signals and command queue.
5. Hold one required readiness input in its bad condition and issue another start
   directive.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the external indicators and LED6 are initially inactive.
2. Verify the accepted start enables the external indicators and LED6.
3. Verify the indicator outputs are enabled before the HVPS start command is queued.
4. Verify stop disables both indicator outputs before the HVPS stop command is queued.
5. Verify a start with a required readiness input bad enables neither indicator output
   and queues no HVPS start command.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-7
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-94
TITLE: Interlocks
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify physical interlock reporting and verify that an open emergency-stop interlock
prevents entry into conditioning and produces a typed interlock fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is on in the cold state and ready to accept a conditioning request.
2. The Services and fault-log screens are available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Open the base emergency-stop interlock and request conditioning.
2. Inspect the system state, fault log, heater command, and coolant-pump command.
3. Restore the base emergency-stop interlock, clear the fault, and repeat steps 1 and 2
   with the remote emergency-stop interlock open.
4. Restore and clear the system.
5. In turn, change the condition of the ion-pump, KUKA readiness, door, and coolant-level
   interlocks.
6. After each change, open the Services screen and wait at least 1 second for status
   reporting.
7. Record the physical-interlock status, required-interlock mask, and any reported fault.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify neither open emergency-stop input permits a transition from cold to
   conditioning.
2. Verify each rejected transition reports a ``FAULT_INTERLOCK`` record containing
   ``Cannot condition with e-stops open``.
3. Verify rejection occurs before a conditioning heater command or coolant-pump start.
4. Verify every changed physical interlock is reported in the Services screen within
   1 second.
5. Verify an interlock selected by the current required-interlock mask produces an
   interlock fault, while an input omitted from that mask remains reported without
   independently producing a fault.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-8
  ROLE: Verifies

