[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-103
TITLE: Operation 09: Initiation
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user runs an ordinary treatment plan and clicks Beam On, the system enters Launching
before emission. When a QC session is armed, Launching additionally waits for the head-interface
Active acknowledgment before radiation can start.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run.
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run an emission.
3. For the QC run, the head interface can delay, acknowledge, or reject the Accumulating command.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run an ordinary emission and observe Launching through emission start.
2. Arm a QC session, press Beam On, and delay the head Active acknowledgment.
3. Provide the Active acknowledgment and observe emission start.
4. Repeat while withholding the acknowledgment or returning Error.
5. After the QC fault is reported, send PC Clear Faults and observe the QC response and
   main-to-head desired state.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The ordinary emission enters Launching and starts only after the HVPS setpoint is reached.
2. The QC emission remains in Launching with emission disabled until Active is acknowledged.
3. Exactly one acknowledged Active edge permits QC radiation.
4. A one-second acknowledgment timeout or Error keeps radiation disabled, commands Stopped, and
   reports a QC fault.
5. Clear Faults resets the PC QC response to Idle with zero accumulations and sample counts,
   clears the per-session QC fault latch, and retransmits Stopped until the head reports Stopped,
   Complete, or its retained Error state. It does not allow a stale Active report to start emission.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-16
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-104
TITLE: Operation 08: Ready 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user prepares one emission, verify that entering Ready never starts radiation
without an explicit Beam On action.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run a treatment
2. One scalar emission is staged, confirmed, and plan-released
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Observe the system in Ready without pressing Beam On
2. Press Beam On once
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify no radiation is emitted before Beam On
2. Verify one point-scope release starts exactly one emission
3. Verify completion transitions to Discharge without a second Setup
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-17
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-105
TITLE: Operation 08: Ready 2
STATEMENT: >>>
When two requested QA emissions are run as separate sessions, verify each session requires
its own Beam On action.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run emissions
2. Two scalar QA emissions are available to the PC
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Prepare and Beam On the first session
2. Prepare the second session and wait in Ready
3. Press Beam On for the second session
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the first completion discharges and does not execute the second emission
2. Verify the second session remains non-emitting in Ready
3. Verify the second Beam On starts only the second emission
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-18
  ROLE: Verifies

