[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-109
TITLE: Operation 06 – HVPS Check
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user opens and closes the interlock door, verify FW can cycle HVPS interlocks successfully.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to run
2. The interlock door is open
3. A treatment plan is ready to load into the system
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the interlock door
2. Close the interlock door
3. Load and start to execute the treatment plan
4. Check the system status
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the door is open for a minimum of 1 second to force latched hardware interlock trigger without fault
2. Verify the interlock door is closed
3. Verify the treatment plan is loaded and running successfully
4. Verify that the system performs an HVPS check prior to ramping up high voltage and that the system is able to ramp up high voltage indicating that the interlocks have been cycled appropriately
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-21
  ROLE: Verifies

