[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-113
TITLE: Operation 4: Treatment Plan Confirmation 1
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify a session becomes confirmed only when the singular scalar parameters match the
staged point without an intervening standby timeout or fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is in Staging with one scalar operational point loaded
2. The firmware command and state-transition test harness is available
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Finalize staging and confirm with one altered scalar parameter
2. Confirm again with parameters that exactly match the loaded point
3. Repeat the matching confirmation, then interrupt the session with standby or a fault before plan release
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the altered confirmation is rejected and plan release is denied
2. Verify the matching confirmation is accepted only in Staged
3. Verify the interruption clears confirmation and plan release is denied
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-24
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-31
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-114
TITLE: Operation 05: Treatment Plan Release 1
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user wants to run an emission with the interlock door is open, make sure FW can't run it.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is up and ready to run an emission
2. A treatment plan is loaded and ready to run an emission
3. Interlock door is open
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the interlock door
2. Try to run an emission for the loaded treatment plan by clicking the Beam on button
3. Click the Logs symbol in the left panel of the GUI
4. Check the logs
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the door is open
2. Verify the emission cannot be started because of the open door of interlock
