[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-123
TITLE: Fault Mode 2
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify ordinary fault entry, lossless FIFO state-event dispatch, queue-overflow handling,
and invalid-state crash dispatch.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready for use and a treatment plan is ready to run.
2. An approved debugger or firmware test hook can pause state-machine processing, set the
   queue indices and current state, observe the queue and fault records, and install a
   dispatch recorder for a valid state.
3. High-voltage, emission-interlock, HVPS, coil, pump, indicator, and system-state outputs
   can be observed.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system, wait for cold, press the emergency stop, and inspect the system mode.
2. Release the emergency stop and clear the fault.
3. With a valid state selected, position an empty event queue near its wrap boundary,
   enqueue a known sequence of valid events below capacity, and process the state machine.
4. Pause processing, reset the queue to empty, enqueue
   ``MAX_EVENT_QUEUE_SIZE - 1`` valid events, and capture the queue contents and indices.
5. Attempt to enqueue one additional valid event and inspect the queue and fault records
   before resuming state-machine processing.
6. Clear the fault and reinitialize the fixture. Set the state value to
   ``NUM_SYSTEM_STATES``, enqueue one valid event, process the state machine, and inspect
   the safety outputs and resulting state.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emergency-stop fault enters the state-appropriate safe fault mode.
2. Verify the below-capacity sequence crosses the wrap boundary and each accepted event
   reaches the valid-state dispatch recorder exactly once, in FIFO order.
3. Verify the first ``MAX_EVENT_QUEUE_SIZE - 1`` events are accepted.
4. Verify the additional event is rejected without changing the write index or any
   accepted queue entry, and a ``FAULT_MEMORY`` record containing
   ``State machine event queue overflow`` is latched.
5. Verify resumed processing enters safe fault handling before dispatching another queued
   event.
6. Verify the out-of-range state dispatches the event to the crash handler, disables the
   high-voltage and emission interlocks, commands all HVPS and coil outputs to zero, stops
   the coolant pump and external indicators, and selects the system-crash state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-80
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-124
