[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-137
TITLE: Temperature Monitoring 1
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify temperature-based cabinet-fan control and delayed coolant-pump shutdown.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is in COLD state without active faults
2. A fixture can control reported cabinet temperature and coolant pressure
3. Cabinet-fan drive and coolant-pump enable can be observed
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Apply cabinet temperatures below 18°C, at 20°C, at 25°C, and at 30°C, allowing one
   monitoring cycle after each change
2. With the pump off, apply out-of-range coolant pressure for more than 200 monitoring
   cycles, then restore valid pressure
3. Initiate conditioning and verify the coolant pump is enabled
4. Send a stop command, observe the pump for three minutes, and observe it again after the
   delay expires
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Cabinet-fan drive advances through 3.7 V, 4.1 V, 4.5 V, and 4.9 V at the respective
   temperature bands; downward transitions retain the prior band through 2°C hysteresis
2. No coolant-pressure fault accumulates while the pump is off or appears when conditioning
   starts with valid pressure
3. Conditioning enables the coolant pump and drives its fan at 1.85 V
4. The pump remains enabled for three minutes after stop, then the pump output is
   deasserted and its fan drive is 0 V
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-65
  ROLE: Verifies

