[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-306
TITLE: QC Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware receives a command from the console application, runs emission and records the accumulated values from the QC diodes with support from the headboard
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is powered on, no faults present, and ready to run emission
2. The QC collimator is connected to the x-ray source
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system / prepare system for operation (wait for system to be “Cold” if it is in “Primed” state otherwise warmup will not run)
2. Use the external console to open the quality assurance tab
3. Open “Beam QA” and select any available energy 50/70/100kV
4. Press on “Prepare” and wait until warmup completes
5. Wait until high voltage completes ramp up and the system is in “Ready” state
6. Press on “Beam On” (emission will start) and wait until the emission completes
7. Toggle “Reports” on the top right corner
8. Select the energy and collimator that was just tested
9. Select the latest result and review the Intensity 1 and Intensity 2 values
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system powers on in “Startup” state or is prepared in “Cold” or “Primed” states
2. Dropdown with energies is available (at least one from 50/70/100kV)
3. At least one collimator is present in the table and “Prepare” button is enabled
4. Warmup completes and high voltage is ramping up
5. The “Ready” button is available
6. Emission is ongoing and completed successfully without any interruption
7. The reports’ view appears and energy and collimator dropdowns are enabled
8. The latest QA execution matched the current time (the one just tested) are results available
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-305
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-307
TITLE: Device Information Version Reporting Through UCSI
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify the device-information exchange from the HVPS interface through main control to UCSI.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. Main-control and HVPS-interface firmware are built with known release version strings.
2. UCSI is installed and connected to the system.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on both boards and start UCSI.
2. Open the UCSI system-status view and observe the main-control and HVPS-interface version information.
3. Refresh the connection so UCSI requests current device information again.
4. Compare the refreshed version information with the installed firmware versions.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Main control obtains the HVPS-interface version after startup.
2. UCSI displays the expected main-control and HVPS-interface release versions and operating modes.
3. Refreshing device information returns the same installed versions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-306
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWMC-308
TITLE: Emission Magnetometer Fault Monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that magnetometer deviations during emission produce a fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. System is ready to run an emission
2. A head-interface simulator can control the magnetometer readings
3. A debugger can observe the magnetometer baseline and deviation counters
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Provide three stable magnetometer packets after the coils are set
2. Start the emission
3. Move one axis beyond the greater of 10% of its baseline or 1.0 uT for two packets, then restore it
4. Move the same axis beyond the limit for three consecutive packets
5. Clear the fault and repeat without providing three post-coil packets
6. Clear the fault and repeat with a non-finite reading during emission
7. Open the system logs
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the post-coil readings are used as the baseline
2. Verify the emission starts without a magnetometer fault
3. Verify no fault is reported and the deviation count is reset
4. Verify the third consecutive deviation reports a magnetometer fault and transitions the system to the fault state
5. Verify a magnetometer fault prevents emission and transitions the system to the fault state
6. Verify a magnetometer fault is reported immediately and transitions the system to the fault state
7. Verify the logs identify the missing sample count or the affected magnetometer, axis, reading, baseline, and limit
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-307
  ROLE: Verifies

[[/SECTION]]
